A weird little trivia: for some time period the Skyking test messages used band names and other pop culture references as the content of test messages. Iron Maiden, The Cure, Duran Duran, Rush, Hansen... And of course test messages may be sent erroneously so we end up with the nuclear command channel carrying messages like "DISREGARD 'THE CURE' TRANSMITTED AT 19" (
https://eam.watch/view/d4272f25-fd33-47a4-9b37-6c55a8ea3d0e
)

Seems like a nice win even if it just does the example they have:
void matmul(Matrix2DFloat A, Matrix2DFloat B, Matrix2DFloat C, int size) {
for (@Parallel int i=0; i<size; i++) {
for (@Parallel int j=0; j<size; j++) {
float sum = 0f;
for (int k=0; k<size; k++)
sum += A.get(i,k)*B.get(k,j);
C.set(i, j, sum);
}
}
}
But the elephant in the room is the Vector API. Is that going to end up like logging - a standardised API nobody uses because it came 10 years late to the party and isn't as good as what was already established?
And why confuse everybody by calling it a VM when it ships as a JAR file that runs in an existing VM?

